WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.421 --> 00:00:03.704
Unit twenty-four. Choking and Severe Bleeding!

2
00:00:04.666 --> 00:00:08.155
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:08.205 --> 00:00:11.223
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:11.273 --> 00:00:15.109
Today we learn about Choking and Severe Bleeding. Let's go!

5
00:00:15.976 --> 00:00:19.009
Choking. Say it with me. Choking!

6
00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:26.523
Back blows. Say it with me. Back blows!

7
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:34.540
Abdominal thrusts. Say it with me. Abdominal thrusts!

8
00:00:38.076 --> 00:00:41.226
Bleeding. Say it with me. Bleeding!

9
00:00:44.673 --> 00:00:48.006
Pressure. Say it with me. Pressure!

10
00:00:51.506 --> 00:00:54.840
Tourniquet. Say it with me. Tourniquet!

11
00:00:58.361 --> 00:01:01.878
Emergency. Say it with me. Emergency!

12
00:01:05.378 --> 00:01:08.545
Training. Say it with me. Training!

13
00:01:12.036 --> 00:01:23.286
For choking, give back blows and abdominal thrusts if trained. For severe bleeding, apply firm pressure; trained responders may use a tourniquet. Call emergency help and consider first aid training.

14
00:01:23.336 --> 00:01:26.155
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:27.302 --> 00:01:32.383
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:32.433 --> 00:01:33.788
Abdominal thrusts!

17
00:01:34.723 --> 00:01:39.827
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:39.877 --> 00:01:41.027
Emergency!

19
00:01:42.053 --> 00:01:48.126
Did you know? A person who is choking may not be able to speak or cough — they may hold their throat!

20
00:01:48.176 --> 00:01:50.061
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:50.811 --> 00:01:58.391
Think and answer. What are the signs that someone is choking?

22
00:01:58.441 --> 00:01:59.591
Great answer!

23
00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:05.020
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.610
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

